# CODEOWNERS - required reviewers per path.
#
# Constitution C8 ("every change is reviewable and reversible") names branch protection
# as part of its enforcement. Branch protection lives in GitHub's settings, not in the
# repository, so the auditable part is kept here and in docs/repo-setup.md.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE RULES BELOW ARE COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE. Replace @OWNER with a real handle or
# team and uncomment them.
#
# Do not leave a placeholder handle in an active rule: GitHub silently IGNORES a
# CODEOWNERS line naming a user or team that cannot review this repository. Combined
# with "Require review from Code Owners" that produces a gate which looks enabled and
# enforces nothing - the exact failure mode this scaffold exists to avoid. An empty
# CODEOWNERS is honestly empty; a broken one lies.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The governance layer. These files decide how everything else is judged, so they
# deserve the strictest review - a weakened constitution or linter silently weakens
# every rule downstream.
# constitution.md            @OWNER
# SPEC_VERSION.md            @OWNER
# sdd.config.yml             @OWNER
# scripts/                   @OWNER
# .github/                   @OWNER
# CLAUDE.md                  @OWNER
# AGENTS.md                  @OWNER

# The living spec and settled decisions.
# docs/spec/                  @OWNER
# docs/adr/                   @OWNER

# Everything else.
# *                           @OWNER
